  "worked_solution": "We start by using the power of product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x{y}^{2})}^{2}\\cdot xy={x}^{2}\\cdot ({y}^{2})^{2}\\cdot xy & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot ({y}^{2})^{2}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{2\\cdot 2}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{4}\\cdot xy & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{4}\\cdot xy & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}\\cdot x)\\cdot ({y}^{4}\\cdot y) & = \\\\ {x}^{2+1}\\cdot {y}^{4+1} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{5} & = \\\\ {x}^{3}{y}^{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
